<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady despite poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady despite poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Thursday, dealers said. Arrivals were poor, estimated around 4,000 tonnes on Thursday.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent prices rose by 100 rupees per tonne but soyoil refined prices were steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady. Soymeal yellow was $270-271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was strong on limited supply.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,450-4,475 rupees per tonne FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
